// A callable read back out of a *mutable* tuple loses its provable storage
// identity.
//
// This is the smallest shape behind `escaping_parameter_stored_into_field.xr`:
// class construction stages field initial values through mutable local slots and
// a tuple, so a callable field always takes this path.
//
// Task340 §3.1 rule 1 lets an `escaping fn(...)` parameter outlive the call, and
// rule 3's prohibitions apply only to non-escaping values, so storing a callable
// in an aggregate is legal. `zero` below is a plain static function reference and
// carries no loans at all.
//
// Expected today (verified on 8862e2576, MSVC Release):
//   callable_through_mutable_tuple.xr:8:15: error: constructed XIR failed
//   checking at function 2 block 4294967295 instruction 7 (status 10)
//
// Contrast, all passing today:
//   - `const t = (zero, 1); var f = t.0` (immutable tuple)
//   - callable through a local variable into `Array.push`
//   - an escaping parameter pushed into an array element
fn zero() -> i64 {
    return 0
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    var t = (zero, 1)
    const f = t.0
    return f()
}
